  "summary_zh": "矮人岩壁由排列整齊的柱狀玄武岩構成，其外形可能受到冰河時期末期海浪侵蝕影響，現為受保護的天然紀念物。\n\n從一號公路旁即可進入步道，參觀時間不長；雨天岩面與草地容易濕滑，請留在既有路線並避免攀爬或破壞岩層。",
  "summary_en": "The Dverghamrar rock formation consists of neatly arranged basalt columns, possibly shaped by glacial meltwater erosion at the end of the Ice Age, and is a protected natural monument. Access the trail from the side of Route 1; the visit is brief. On rainy days the rock surfaces and grass become slippery, so stay on the marked path and avoid climbing or damaging the rocks. Parking is available for free nearby. No restroom facilities are provided. Plan to spend about 30 minutes at the site.",
